34
00:02:27.833 --> 00:02:34.833
Why can't they have anesthesiologists, start prescribing drugs?

35
00:02:34.833 --> 00:02:41.133
Medical misdiagnosis of depression.

36
00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:48.133
That's about One Sigma. Oh my. But, you can see overall the average

37
00:02:48.133 --> 00:02:53.199
from this set of many, many different data points from the medical industry,

38
00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:57.200
is all in that region of about Four Sigma.

39
00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:02.466
With an industry median at about 3.4 Sigma.

40
00:03:02.466 --> 00:03:08.932
Well, we know automobiles is about Four Sigma. Healthcare is about 3.4.

41
00:03:08.933 --> 00:03:13.666
That would tend to say, as a society, we value the quality of our cars

42
00:03:13.666 --> 00:03:16.699
more than we do ourselves.

43
00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:23.600
That’s very, very interesting isn’t it? Well again, benchmarking is another way to bring this out.

44
00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:23.900

